%% The coordinator demo's diagram (coordinator.sh show, chapter 4): how one delegation runs.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Op as operator (agentctl)
    participant D as agentsessionsd
    participant C as coordinator harness<br/>(micro-VM)
    participant M as gpt-5.4-mini<br/>(Azure OpenAI)
    participant X as invocation executor<br/>(in agentsessionsd)
    participant Wk as writer / reviewer harness<br/>(child session, own micro-VM)
    Op->>D: Exec(coordinator session, request)
    D->>C: turn
    C->>M: model call (through agentsessionsd)
    M-->>C: {"invoke": "writer", "task": ...}
    C->>D: tool call agentsuite.invoke
    D->>X: run the call (journaled TOOL_CALL)
    X->>X: edge declared? maxConcurrent, maxDepth
    X->>D: CreateSession + Exec on the writer harness
    D->>Wk: child turn
    Wk-->>X: reply
    X-->>C: TOOL_RESULT (child session, reply)
    C->>D: tool call to reviewer, REQUIRES_APPROVAL
    D-->>Op: APPROVAL_REQUEST; turn parked
    Op->>D: approve / deny
    D->>X: approved: child session on reviewer
    D-->>C: denied: TOOL_RESULT APPROVAL_DENIED
